senses.gloss:
सम्-उच्-√ चर् (-उद्-√ चर्) P. -चरति, to go out together, Nir.;
to go up, be borne upwards, ascend, MW.;
to utter, pronounce, repeat, HPariś. :
Caus. -चारयति, to utter sounds together, talk together, MW.

सम्-उच्-√ चि (-उद्- √ 1. चि) P. Ā. -चिनोति, -चिनुते (ind.p. -चयित्वा), to heap or pile up together, accumulate, add together, MBh.;
to collect, gather, arrange in order, Baudh. :
Desid. See सम्-उच्चिचीषा.

सम्-उच्-छ्वस् (-उद्-√ श्वस्) P. -छ्वसिति, or -छ्वसति, to breathe well or regularly, Suśr.;
to breathe again, recover, revive, Kathās.;
to spring or sprout up, Śiś. :
Caus. See सम्-उच्छ्वासित.

सम्-उज्-√ जृम्भ् (-उद्-√ जृम्भ्) Ā. -ज्रिम्भते, to gape wide open, be extended or spread out, Mṛcch.;
to burst forth, become visible, arise, Prab., Sch.;
to begin, be about to (inf.), Bhartṛ.

सम्-उत्-√ क्षिप् P. Ā. -क्षिपति, ˚ते, to throw or raise or lift up, MBh.; Pañcat.; MārkP.;
to throw or scatter about, throw aside, loosen, R.;
to liberate, Pañcat.;
to waste, destroy, R.

सम्-उत्-√ खन् P. Ā. -खनति, ˚ते (ind.p. -खाय), to dig up by the roots, Kauś.;
to eradicate, exterminate or destroy utterly, Prab.;
to draw forth, draw (a sword), Prasannar.

सम्-उत्-√ तॄ P. -तरति (ind.p. -तीर्य), to pass or come out of (abl.; with or without जलात्, ‘to step or emerge out of the water’), GṛS.; MBh. &c.;
to escape from, get rid of (abl.), MBh.; R. &c.;
to break through, pass over or beyond, cross over, cross, ib.

सम्-उत्-था (-उद्-√ स्था) P. Ā. -तिष्ठति, ˚ते, to rise up together, Jātakam.;
to rise up (as from death), get up (from sleep &c.), ŚBr.; MBh. &c.;
to recover (from sickness), Car.;
to rise (in the sky), gather (as clouds), MBh.; Kathās.;
to come forth, spring from (abl.), appear, become visible, ŚBr. &c. &c.;
to arise for action, prepare for or to (loc. or inf.), MBh.; VarBṛS. :
Caus. -थापयति to cause to rise together, lift or raise up, elevate, MBh.; R.; BhP.;
to awaken, excite, arouse, R.; Jātakam.

सम्-उत्-√ पत् P. -पतति, to fly up together, spring up, ascend, rise (as the sun, clouds &c.), AV. &c. &c.;
to rush upon, attack, assail, Kām.;
to rush out of, burst forth, MBh.;
to arise, appear, ib.;
to fly away, depart, disappear, Pañcat. :
Desid. See below.

सम्-उत्-√ सृज् P. -सृजति, to pour out or send forth together, hurl, throw, shoot oft (arrows), R.;
to give forth, emit, discharge (urine &c.), shed (tears), utter (a curse &c.), Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to leave or abandon or completely put aside, put off or down, throw into (loc.), ib.;
to let loose, release, ib.;
to give up, renounce (together or at the same time), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to deliver over, present to (dat.), give, R.; Hcat.

सम्-उद्-आ-√ चर् Ā. -चरते, to move or travel about (e.g. रथेन, ‘in a chariot’), Siddh.;
 P. -चरति, to act towards, treat, MBh.;
to practise, accomplish, do, ib.;
to speak to, address, Divyāv.

सम्-उद्-आ-√ वह् P. -वहति, to lead or conduct out, draw or carry away, Hariv.;
to draw along (said of horses), R.;
to conduct home, marry, MBh.

सम्-उद्-√ ईर् Caus. -ईरयति, to drive out, expel, MBh.;
to raise (dust), MBh.;
to hurl, throw, ib.;
to utter, speak, declare, Kathās.

सम्-उद्-√ दिश् P. -दिशति (ind.p. दिश्य, q.v.), to point out or indicate fully, mention at full, state, declare, communicate, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to designate as, name (two acc.), VarBṛS.;
to enter into discussion with (instr.), AitĀr.;
to refer or relate to (see next).

2. सम्-उद्-धृ (-उद्-√ हृ) P. Ā. -उद्धरति, ˚ते, to take quite out, draw well out, extract from (abl.), Kauś.; MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to root out, extirpate, exterminate, destroy utterly, MBh.;
to rescue, save, deliver from (abl.), MBh.; Jātakam.; Pañcat.;
to lift, hold up, MBh.; Mṛcch.;
to pick up (a coin), Hit.;
to raise up, strengthen, restore, MBh.;
to divide, Bījag.; R. &c. :
Desid. See सम्-उज्-जिहीर्षु (s.v.)

सम्-उद्-√ वह् P. Ā. -वहति, ˚ते, to lift out, carry forth, Bhaṭṭ.;
to lead away, lead home, marry, Yājñ.; R.; BhP.;
to lift up, raise, MBh.;
to bear (with मनसा, or हृदयेन, ‘in the heart’), tolerate, suffer, endure, MBh.; R.; Kathās.;
to wear, possess, Ratnāv.;
to exhibit, show, display, R.; VarBṛS.

सम्-उन्-√ नी (-उद्-√ नी) P. Ā. -नयति, ˚ते, to lead or conduct upward, together, raise completely up, elevate, increase, MBh.; BhP.;
to instigate, stimulate, Kām.;
to deduce, infer, Rājat.; Sāh.;
to pay off (a debt), Kull. on Mn. ix, 107.

सम्-उन्-√ मील् (-उद्-√ मील्) P. -मीलति, to become fully expanded or unfolded or displayed, Amar.; Prab. :
Caus. -मीलयति to open (the eyes), MBh.; R.;
to expand, display, exhibit, Uttarar.

सम्-उप-√ जन् Ā. -जायते, to arise, spring up, take place, Kāv.;
to be born again, MBh. :
Caus. -जनयति, to generate, cause, produce, Ṛtus.

सम्-उप-√ नी P. Ā. -नयति, ˚ते, to lead up to together, bring or draw near to, lead to (acc.), MBh.; Kāv.; VarBṛS.;
to take away, carry off, MBh.;
to offer (a sacrifice), R.;
to bring about, cause, Hariv.

सम्-उप-√ पद् Ā. -पद्यते, to come to pass, be brought about or accomplished, MBh.;
to meet with (acc.), experience, ib. :
Caus. -पादयति, to bring about, make ready, prepare, R.

सम्-उप-√ या P. -याति, to go up to or approach (with acc.), R.;
to betake one's self to (acc.), MBh.; VarBṛS.;
to go to any state or condition (with acc.), VarBṛS.

सम्-उप-√ विश् P. -विशति, to sit down together or near, sit down on (loc. acc., or gen. with उपरि), ŚBr.; GṛŚrS.; ChUp. &c.;
to lie down upon (acc.), ib.;
to encamp, ib.;
to oversleep (the right time for anything), R. :
Caus. -वेशयति, to cause to sit down, ask to be seated, Hit.;
to cause to encamp, Rājat.

सम्-उप-√ स्था P. Ā. -तिष्ठति, ˚ते, to stand near (at any one's service), R.;
to lean on (acc.), ib.;
to go to, approach (acc.), MBh.;
to occur, arise, befall, Śak. :
Caus. स्थापयति, to set up, Suśr.

सम्-उप-√ स्पृश् P. -स्पृशति, to touch, R.;
to touch (water for ablution), touch with water (instr.), bathe in (loc.), MBh.; Yājñ.;
to sip water, MW.

सम्-उप-√ हृ P. Ā. -हरति, ˚ते, to bring towards, offer, R.; Jātakam.;
to pay (honour), Jātakam.;
to perform (a sacrifice), MW.

सम्-उपा-√ हृ P. Ā. -हरति, ˚ते, to bring near, fetch, procure, MBh.; R. &c.;
to offer, sacrifice, MBh.; R.; BhP.;
to sacrifice one's self, Rājat.;
to enter upon (initiation), R.

सम्-उपा-√ दा Ā. -दत्ते (ind.p. -दाय, q.v.), to gain, receive, acquire, MBh.; MārkP.;
to take away from, deprive of MBh.;
to collect, heap together, R.;
to assume, put on MBh.

सम्-उपास् (-उप-√ आस्) Ā. -उपास्ते (pr. p. -उपासीन), to sit near together or near each other, R.;
to engage in or devote one's self to anything together, practise in common (or singly), Gṛhyās.; R.;
to serve or honour together, revere, worship, adore, MBh.; Mṛcch.; Ragh.

सम्-उपे (-उप- √ 5. इ) -उपैति, to come together, meet (as friends or foes), MBh.; R.; Pañcat.;
to have sexual intercourse, MBh.;
to come near, approach, go to (acc.), ib. ;
 to have recourse to, apply to, ŚārṅgP.;
to attain, incur, partake of VarBṛS.; Śiś.;
to occur, happen, appear, MBh.;
to come upon, befall, R.;
to be absorbed in RPrāt.

सम्-उल्-√ लस् (-उद्-√ लस्) P. -लसति, to shine forth, gleam, glitter, Śiś.;
to break forth, appear, Kir.; Pañcat.;
to sound, resound, Prasannar. :
Caus. -लासयति, to cause to jump or sport, exhilarate, make glad, MW.

सम्-उल्-√ लिख् (-उद्-√ लिख्) P. -लिखति, to scratch up all round, dig up, ŚBr.;
to scratch, furrow, Kum.;
to rub against, graze, R.;
to write down, mention (in a book), L.

सम्-√ मुह् P. -मुह्यति (pf. -मुमोह, or -मुमुह्स्), to become quite stupefied or bewildered or unconscious, MBh.; R.; BhP.;
to become confused or unrecognizable (as the quarters of the sky), MBh.:
Caus. -मोहयति, to stupefy, make unconscious, perplex, bewilder, lead astray, MBh.; Kāv. &c.

सम्-√ मुर्छ् (or -मूर्छ्) P. -मूर्छति, to congeal into a fixed form, become dense, thicken, coagulate, Kāv.; VarBṛS.; Suśr.;
to become stupid or senseless (see -मूर्छित);
to acquire consistency or firmness or strength, increase, expand, become powerful, make a loud sound, Ragh. :
Caus. -मूर्छयति, to cause to assume consistency, form, fashion (see -मूर्छित-वत्);
to stupefy, cause to faint, Uttarar.

सम्-√ मुर्छ् (or -मूर्छ्) P. -मूर्छति, to congeal into a fixed form, become dense, thicken, coagulate, Kāv.; VarBṛS.; Suśr.;
to become stupid or senseless (see -मूर्छित);
to acquire consistency or firmness or strength, increase, expand, become powerful, make a loud sound, Ragh. :
Caus. -मूर्छयति, to cause to assume consistency, form, fashion (see -मूर्छित-वत्);
to stupefy, cause to faint, Uttarar.
